@startuml model-access-today
' ONE file, TWO diagrams. This one = the gap AS IT WAS; below = the fix, BUILT 2026-08-13
' (see planning/platform/model-access-port.md).
title BEFORE - two paths to models, one hole (fixed - see second diagram)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
left to right direction

rectangle "Brain (agent loop)" as brain
rectangle "chat-shaped tools\n(verify_figure, ...)\ntext/images in -> TEXT out" as chattools

rectangle "GOVERNED FUNNEL" as funnel #E8F5E9 {
  rectangle "resolve_tool_model\n(one config seam: agent.toml\n-> plugins.*.tools.*.model)" as seam
  rectangle "oneshot.vision_complete" as oneshot
  rectangle "LiteLLM" as litellm
}

rectangle "ROGUE PATH" as roguebox #FFEBEE {
  rectangle "image-bytes-out tools\ngenerate_artwork / edit_artwork\nread_labels / extract_annotations\nvectorize" as rogue
  rectangle "resolve_key()\n(copy-pasted per plugin)" as rk
  rectangle "env GEMINI_API_KEY\n(daemon process env)" as env
  rectangle "google-genai SDK\n(direct call)" as sdk
}

cloud "model proxy (cloud modes)\nsession token -> metered\nper account" as proxy
cloud "provider direct (local BYOK)\nuser's own key" as byok
cloud "Google API\nunmetered, unbilled" as google #FFEBEE

brain --> seam
chattools --> seam
seam --> oneshot
oneshot --> litellm
litellm --> proxy : desktop cloud /\nweb hosted
litellm --> byok : local BYOK

rogue --> rk
rk --> env
rk --> sdk
sdk --> google

note bottom of env #FFCDD2
  THE GAP
  local: works (key in your env)
  hosted: daemon holds NO raw keys
  -> "no Gemini API key" failure
  and even WITH a key: bypasses
  metering + per-account billing
end note
@enduml


@startuml model-access-fixed
title BUILT (2026-08-13) - one ModelAccess port; mode decided once; sandbox makes it the only door

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
left to right direction

rectangle "ANY tool declaring needs_model\n(brain, chat tools, image tools,\nagent-builder plugin tools)" as anytool

rectangle "ModelAccess port (INJECTED)\ncomplete() / vision_complete()\ngenerate_image() / embed()\ntools get the handle, never a key" as port #C8E6C9

rectangle "container builds it ONCE per mode\n(zero if-hosted branching in plugins)" as factory #C8E6C9

cloud "local BYOK\nprovider direct, user's keys" as byok
cloud "desktop cloud / web hosted\nLiteLLM proxy + session token\nchat routes + gemini PASSTHROUGH\n(image-gen & grounding metered too)" as proxy

rectangle "UNTRUSTED plugins (agent-builder made)\nagents/ID/plugins/" as untrusted #FFFDE7 {
  rectangle "sandbox subprocess\nenv SCRUBBED: no *_API_KEY\negress allowlist: provider domains blocked" as sbx #FFF9C4
  rectangle "CapabilityResolver grant\n(reads needs_model / model_kind\noff the tool contract)" as grant #FFF9C4
}

anytool --> port
port --> factory
factory --> byok : mode = local
factory --> proxy : mode = cloud / hosted

sbx --> grant
grant --> port : model calls cross the trust\nboundary as RPC to the\ndaemon's port

note bottom of sbx #FFF9C4
  ENFORCEMENT, not convention:
  no keys in env + no egress
  -> the injected port is the ONLY
  door, and everything through it
  is mode-correct and metered.
  First-party plugins comply by
  template; third-party because
  there is no other path.
end note
@enduml
